Software this project needs, and does not include
-------------------------------------------------
The Python packages listed in `requirements.txt` (FastAPI, Uvicorn, HTTPX, pytest and the Anthropic SDK) are
installed by whoever runs the project, each under its own licence. None of them is copied into this repository.
The engine itself uses the Python standard library only.

The AI layer and the model
--------------------------
The server in live mode, and the scripts that record answers or run the benchmark, call a model of Anthropic
through its API, with the key of whoever runs them. No model and no key is part of this repository.
`ai/recorded/` is where answers of that model are kept once they have been recorded: its README says how they are
made, and how they are played again and checked.

